%feature("docstring") add_unhappy_atom_marker_py "
add an \"unhappy atom\" marker on the given atom

The marker is a camera-facing sad-face image drawn at the position of the specified atom, used to flag problem atoms. If imol is not a valid model molecule, or the atom spec is malformed or does not match an atom, this function does nothing.

  imol  the molecule index   atom_spec_list  a 5-member atom spec: [chain-id, res-no, ins-code, atom-name, alt-conf], e.g. [\"A\", 145, \"\", \"CE\", \"\"]

Parameters
----------
imol : int
    the molecule index
atom_spec_list : object
    a 5-member atom spec: [chain-id, res-no, ins-code, atom-name, alt-conf], e.g. [\"A\", 145, \"\", \"CE\", \"\"]
";

%feature("docstring") remove_unhappy_atom_marker_py "
remove the \"unhappy atom\" marker from the given atom

The marker at the current position of the specified atom is removed. Note that markers store positions, not atom specs - so if the atom has moved since the marker was added (e.g. by refinement) the marker will not be found (use remove_all_unhappy_atom_markers() in that case).

  imol  the molecule index   atom_spec_list  a 5-member atom spec: [chain-id, res-no, ins-code, atom-name, alt-conf]

Parameters
----------
imol : int
    the molecule index
atom_spec_list : object
    a 5-member atom spec: [chain-id, res-no, ins-code, atom-name, alt-conf]
";

